# Family House Connect Mobile — environment notes

Flutter does not load `.env` at runtime. Pass compile-time defines:

```sh
flutter run --dart-define-from-file=dart-define.example.json
```

Or individually:

```sh
flutter run \
  --dart-define=FHC_API_URL=https://familyconnect.katakarra.com/api/v1
```

Local Laravel: `--dart-define-from-file=dart-define.local.json`

## URL defines (aligned)

| Define | Meaning | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `FHC_API_URL` | Full Laravel `/api/v1` base used by app transport/auth | `https://familyconnect.katakarra.com/api/v1` |
| `FHC_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL` | Host origin for generated `api/clients/dart` public client (no `/api/v1`) | `https://familyconnect.katakarra.com` |

Either define is enough. `resolveFhcApiUrl` / `resolveFhcPublicApiBaseUrl` convert between them.

When both are unset the production host is used. Release builds refuse loopback URLs (`localhost`, `10.0.2.2`).

## Flutter web (Chrome) vs production API

Running `flutter run -d chrome` against `https://familyconnect.katakarra.com` is a **cross-origin**
browser request. If the API has not deployed the loopback CORS patterns, Chrome shows
`ClientException: Failed to fetch` — not invalid credentials.

Prefer **Android emulator, iOS simulator, or Windows desktop** for production API testing.
For web dev, use local Laravel:

```sh
flutter run -d chrome --dart-define=FHC_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1
```

Ensure Laravel `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS` includes your Flutter web origin if you use a custom port.

## Mobile auth endpoints (Bearer + `X-Device-Identifier`)

Base: `{FHC_API_URL}` → typically `…/api/v1`

| Method | Path | Auth |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/mobile/auth/login` | body `device_identifier` |
| POST | `/mobile/auth/refresh` | body refresh + `device_identifier` |
| POST | `/mobile/auth/logout` | Bearer + `X-Device-Identifier` |
| POST | `/mobile/auth/mfa/challenge` | Bearer + `X-Device-Identifier` |
| POST | `/mobile/auth/mfa/totp/setup` | Bearer + `X-Device-Identifier` |
| POST | `/mobile/auth/mfa/totp/confirm` | Bearer + `X-Device-Identifier` |

Protected feature calls use the same Bearer + device headers via `HttpApiTransport`.

## Visual review only

`FHC_VISUAL_REVIEW=true` enables the allow-all authorization gateway for golden/screenshot suites. **Ignored in release builds** — never ships unbound fixtures or allow-all auth.
